---
import DocsLayout from "../../components/docs/DocsLayout.astro";
import { PACK_FACTS } from "../../components/docs/facts";
import LayerDiagram from "../../components/docs/LayerDiagram.astro";
import LinkCard from "../../components/docs/LinkCard.astro";
import QueryResults from "../../components/docs/QueryResults.astro";
import { DASHBOARD_URL } from "../../config";
---

<DocsLayout path="/docs/">
  <p>Emojisense gives your product everything emoji in one platform. People type what they mean, in their own words and language, and get the right emoji. Messages get reaction suggestions. Photos turn into emoji. Your own custom emoji sit next to Unicode, and every device can show the same emoji art.</p>

  <QueryResults
    queries={[
      { query: "jurassic park", note: "a film" },
      { query: "greatest of all time", note: "slang" },
      { query: "hallowelen", note: "a typo" },
      { query: "kolay gelsin", locale: "tr", note: "Turkish" },
      { query: "feliz cumpleaños", locale: "es", note: "Spanish" },
    ]}
  />
  <p>These results come from the real engine and the shipped data, computed when this page was built. The same engine runs in your users’ browsers.</p>

  <h2 id="what-you-can-build">What you can build</h2>
  <ul class="docs-cards">
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/guides/search/" emoji="🔎" title="Search in your picker" description="Rank emoji by meaning on every keystroke, in any picker." />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/guides/reactions/" emoji="🙌" title="Reaction suggestions" description="Suggest the reactions a message deserves." />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/guides/photo-to-emoji/" emoji="📸" title="Photo to emoji" description="Turn a photo into fitting emoji. The image is never stored." />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/guides/custom-emoji/" emoji="🦄" title="Custom emoji" description="Your own emoji, searchable next to Unicode." />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/guides/emoji-sets/" emoji="🎨" title="Hosted emoji sets" description="Twemoji, Noto or Fluent from the edge." />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/guides/analytics/" emoji="📈" title="Analytics" description="What people search for, and what finds nothing." />
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>Teams, tenants and webhooks complete the platform for products with many customers. See the <a href="/docs/guides/teams/">guides</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="how-it-fits">How it fits together</h2>
  <p>Emojisense answers each search in the cheapest place that can answer it well. Most searches never leave the device. Only the unsure ones go to the edge, and the edge result merges in without moving the confident hits.</p>
  <LayerDiagram />
  <p>The engine is a small, dependency-free package. The data packs hold {PACK_FACTS.emojiCount?.toLocaleString("en")} emoji (Emoji {PACK_FACTS.emojiVersion}) with aliases in {PACK_FACTS.languages} languages. The English core pack is about {PACK_FACTS.englishCoreKb} KB compressed, and the extension pack with more aliases and typos loads when the browser is idle. Read <a href="/docs/concepts/">Concepts</a> for the details.</p>

  <h2 id="pick-an-integration">Pick an integration</h2>
  <p>Every integration uses the same engine, packs and API. Pick the one that matches your stack.</p>
  <ul class="docs-cards">
    <li>
      <LinkCard id="react-frimousse" href="/docs/integrations/react/" emoji="⚛️" title="React and Frimousse" description="Hooks, a drop-in picker and a shadcn/ui component." meta="@emojisense/react" />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard id="web-component" href="/docs/integrations/web-component/" emoji="🧩" title="Web component" description="Vue, Svelte, Angular and plain HTML." meta="@emojisense/web-component" />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard id="vanilla" href="/docs/sdk/" emoji="📦" title="Plain JavaScript" description="The engine alone, for any runtime and any UI." meta="emojisense" />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/integrations/tiptap/" emoji="✍️" title="Tiptap" description="Type a colon, get emoji ranked by meaning." meta="@emojisense/tiptap" />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/integrations/lexical/" emoji="📝" title="Lexical" description="Colon autocomplete for Lexical in React." meta="@emojisense/lexical" />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/integrations/ckeditor5/" emoji="🖋️" title="CKEditor 5" description="Colon autocomplete on the Mention plugin." meta="@emojisense/ckeditor5" />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/integrations/tinymce/" emoji="📄" title="TinyMCE" description="Colon autocomplete for TinyMCE 7 and 8." meta="@emojisense/tinymce" />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/integrations/emoji-mart/" emoji="🗃️" title="emoji-mart" description="Keep emoji-mart, add Emojisense ranking." meta="@emojisense/emoji-mart" />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/integrations/swift/" emoji="🍎" title="Swift" description="iOS and macOS, same results as TypeScript." meta="Swift Package" />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/integrations/mcp/" emoji="🤖" title="MCP server" description="Emoji tools for AI assistants. Offline by default." meta="@emojisense/mcp" />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/integrations/chrome/" emoji="🌐" title="Chrome extension" description="A picker for any text field on the web." />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/integrations/raycast/" emoji="🔦" title="Raycast" description="Search emoji and paste them into any app." />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/integrations/wordpress/" emoji="📰" title="WordPress" description="Block editor, reactions, comments, bbPress and BuddyPress." meta="Plugin" />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/integrations/discourse/" emoji="💬" title="Discourse" description="Composer, chat and picker search by meaning." meta="Theme component" />
    </li>
    <li>
      <LinkCard href="/docs/integrations/http/" emoji="🔌" title="HTTP" description="Any language, any server, with plain HTTP." />
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="start">Start in five minutes</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/docs/quickstart/">Quickstart</a> takes you from a key to a working picker. You can start without a key: the API then applies a stricter rate limit. The Free plan needs no card. Get a key from the <a href={`${DASHBOARD_URL}/`}>dashboard</a> when you are ready. To try search, reactions and photos first, open the <a href="/playground/">playground</a>.</p>
</DocsLayout>
